<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch Q2 GDP rises 2.8 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Dutch Q2 GDP rises 2.8 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>VOORBURG, Netherlands 1996-08-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch second quarter gross domestic product (GDP) rose a provisional 2.8 percent year-on-year, the Central Bureau of Statistics (CBS) said on Thursday.  </p>
<p>DUTCH GDP</p>
<p>		    Q2 96	 Q1 96	 Q4 95	 Q3 95</p>
<p> year-on-year   +2.8	  +1.8	  +1.6	  +2.1</p>
<p>vs previous qtr</p>
<p> (seas. adj.)   +1.3	  +0.9	  +0.3	  +0.2</p>
<p>Note - Figures show real percent changes.  </p>
<p>The CBS said job creation as a result of wage restraints was a major factor behind the good economic performance compared with neighbouring economies such as Germany, Belgium and France.</p>
<p>&quot;The wage restraint deal since late 1992 is having its effect,&quot; spokesman Peter Oomens said.</p>
